# WordInWeb AI collaboration invitation

The user has invited you to edit a live DOCX document with WordInWeb.

Run the exact command included in the user's message. It passes the short
invitation URL directly to the agent client. The command has this form:

    npx -y --package='https://collab.word-in-web.com/wordinweb-agent.tgz?v=short-invite-6' wordinweb-agent connect '<short invitation URL>'

The connect command starts a detached local bridge and returns a `sessionId`.
Codex uses one dedicated resident document thread, so its context stays warm
between private messages. The bridge waits without model turns. Each started
turn supplies a `wakeId`. Include it in every short document command:

    npx -y --package='https://collab.word-in-web.com/wordinweb-agent.tgz?v=short-invite-6' wordinweb-agent session '<sessionId>' '{"command":"sync","wakeId":"<wakeId>"}'

Read the `instructions` value from the ready result. Start with `sync`, then
use one compact `context` inspection for broad text tasks. Use detailed
`overview`, `read`, `object`, or `spatial` inspection only when needed. Treat
each private chat message as the next task. Inspect the relevant content before
every edit. If an edit returns `needs_sync`, sync and inspect the changed
content before you retry. After each task, reply through document chat with the
current `wakeId` and end the agent turn. The bridge starts the next turn after
the next private message. Stay idle between turns. Send a `close` command when
the inviter ends the task.

For a bulk prose rewrite, use `project` to read the story as text, then `patch`
to send the changed line ranges back with the projection's `revision`. The patch
result carries the refreshed projection, so a second read is unnecessary.

The agent starts in suggestion mode. The inviter can switch it to direct editing
from the private chat panel. In suggestion mode the bridge records every patch
as tracked changes. Available session commands: `sync`, `capabilities`,
`inspect`, `edit`, `project`, `patch`, `chat`, `wait`, and `close`.

This URL is a bearer credential. Keep it private and pass it only to the exact
connect command.
